[P0128 B] The integer stack fast path wraps out-of-range Lua integers into u8. src/conversion.rs:864. The optimized FromLua::from_stack implementation for narrow integer types accepts a successful lua_tointegerx conversion as sufficient and truncates the resulting Lua integer to the Rust target type. Thus evaluating "return 256" as u8 succeeds with 0 and evaluating "return -1" succeeds with 255, rather than returning FromLuaConversionError. Rust callers receiving numeric Lua results can silently accept values outside the requested type's range.


